4. Pseudocode
START

Read the input folder
Create a ConcurrentLinkedQueue for results
Create a fixed thread pool

FOR each expected score file
    Create a Callable task

    Inside the task:
        TRY
            Read the file
            Validate student ID and marks
            Calculate total marks
            Create a successful result
        CATCH any file or validation exception
            Create a failure result

        Add the result to the concurrent collection
        RETURN the result

    Submit the task to ExecutorService
    Store its Future
END FOR

FOR each Future
    Wait for the task to complete
    Handle any unexpected task exception
END FOR

Count successful results
Count failed results
Print the final summary
Measure total processing time

Shutdown ExecutorService

STOP




Stage 3 – Implement and Measure (Student B) – 3 Marks
1. Java implementation
Input file format

Each score file contains one line with a student ID and three subject marks, separated by commas.

Example: score00001.txt
STU001,80,75,90


The program validates the file and calculates the total marks. It treats missing files, invalid data and reading errors as individual failures.

import java.io.*;
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

class Result {
    String fileName;
    String studentId;
    boolean success;
    int totalMarks;
    String message;

    Result(String fileName, String studentId,
           boolean success, int totalMarks, String message) {
        this.fileName = fileName;
        this.studentId = studentId;
        this.success = success;
        this.totalMarks = totalMarks;
        this.message = message;
    }
}

class ScoreProcessor implements Callable<Result> {
    private File file;

    ScoreProcessor(File file) {
        this.file = file;
    }

    public Result call() {
        try (BufferedReader br =
                 new BufferedReader(new FileReader(file))) {

            String line = br.readLine();

            if (line == null || line.trim().isEmpty()) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Empty file");
            }

            String[] data = line.split(",");

            if (data.length != 4) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                    "Invalid file format");
            }

            String studentId = data[0].trim();

            if (studentId.isEmpty()) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                    "Missing student ID");
            }

            int total = 0;

            for (int i = 1; i < 4; i++) {
                int mark = Integer.parseInt(data[i].trim());

                if (mark < 0 || mark > 100) {
                    throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                        "Invalid mark: " + mark);
                }

                total += mark;
            }

            return new Result(file.getName(), studentId,
                true, total, "Processed successfully");

        } catch (Exception e) {
            return new Result(file.getName(), "",
                false, 0, e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}

public class ResultProcessingSystem {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        String folder = args.length > 0 ? args[0] : "scores";
        int poolSize = args.length > 1
                ? Integer.parseInt(args[1]) : 4;

        ConcurrentLinkedQueue<Result> results =
                new ConcurrentLinkedQueue<>();

        ExecutorService executor =
                Executors.newFixedThreadPool(poolSize);

        List<Future<Result>> futures = new ArrayList<>();

        long start = System.nanoTime();

        try {
            // Attempt all 10,000 expected files
            for (int i = 1; i <= 10000; i++) {

                String fileName =
                    String.format("score%05d.txt", i);

                File file = new File(folder, fileName);

                Future<Result> future =
                    executor.submit(new ScoreProcessor(file));

                futures.add(future);
            }

            // Wait for every submitted task
            for (Future<Result> future : futures) {
                try {
                    Result result = future.get();
                    results.add(result);

                } catch (ExecutionException e) {
                    results.add(new Result(
                        "Unknown task", "", false, 0,
                        "Unexpected task failure: " +
                        e.getCause()
                    ));
                }
            }

        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
            System.out.println("Processing was interrupted.");

        } finally {
            executor.shutdown();
        }

        long end = System.nanoTime();

        int success = 0;
        int failure = 0;

        for (Result r : results) {
            if (r.success) {
                success++;
            } else {
                failure++;
            }
        }

        System.out.println("\n--- SEMESTER RESULT SUMMARY ---");
        System.out.println("Thread Pool Size: " + poolSize);
        System.out.println("Total Processed: " + results.size());
        System.out.println("Successful Files: " + success);
        System.out.println("Failed Files: " + failure);
        System.out.printf("Execution Time: %.3f ms%n",
                (end - start) / 1_000_000.0);

        if (results.size() == 10000) {
            System.out.println("Summary Check: PASSED");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Summary Check: INCOMPLETE");
        }
    }
}



Important implementation note: This code attempts all 10,000 expected filenames, even when some files are missing. Each Callable catches file-reading and validation exceptions and returns a failure result. The main thread collects every returned result through its Future.
